def handle_request(req):
    // Declared agents get clean structured JSON + discounted compute, removing the incentive to spoof.
    if req.headers.has('X-Agent-Delegation-Proof') and verify_principal_signature(req):
        // Attribution and consent are cryptographically asserted by the user's delegate token, not a visual CMP.
        return serve_machine_api(req, record_touchpoint=req.token.provenance, billable_unit='token_rate')

    // 2. Undeclared traffic: measure interaction physics to build empirical ground truth, not just block.
    interaction_profile = extract_physics_telemetry(req) // micro-latencies, DOM read patterns, event dispatch authenticity
    if interaction_profile.confidence_human < THRESHOLD:
        // Do not hard-block; blocking triggers adversarial evasion. Strip ad beacons to prevent ad fraud.
        log_unlabeled_agent_sample(req) // Creates the industry's missing baseline dataset
        return serve_static_ssr(req, suppress_ads=True, suppress_consent_banner=True)

    // 3. Human path: standard visual experience with active ad tracking certified by interactive proof-of-view.
    return serve_interactive_web(req, enable_ad_pixels=True)

Hush, don’t chase IP-address ghosts or trust a browser’s name;
That arms race sorts by likelihood, but cannot prove a claim.

Invite agents, shops, and users to a measured little trial;
Label every journey end to end, then audit every mile.

Test signed, short-lived permission: user, purpose, consent, scope;
Log touchpoints by assurance, not attribution dressed as hope.

Give unknown traffic narrower rights, not secret prices or a ban;
Without shared trust and incentives, we’re still dreaming of a plan.
